files.change:
Add one unlayered rule immediately before the existing `/* Below 480px a card has no border ... */` block:

    /*
     * The skip link leaves the clip when it takes focus and takes its place in the flow, so it needs
     * a margin of its own to clear the header below it. `focus:mb-space-2` in its class list loses:
     * `not-sr-only` sets `margin: 0`, both live in @layer utilities, and utilities sort by property
     * so margin is emitted first. An unlayered rule outranks every layered one whatever the order.
     */
    .skip-link:focus {
      margin-bottom: var(--spacing-space-2);
    }

Place it with the other unlayered element rules, not inside @theme. Change NOTHING else: the six --spacing-space-N tokens and their explanatory comment are correct and QA's T-11 confirms they generate the utilities; the ten colour tokens, --radius, the font stacks, the five text sizes, the heading sizes, the focus-ring block and the 480px card rule are all correct and all unchanged by this.

